'=============================================================================================
' -- EDIT file, the 6502DOS Editor
' -- edits a text file on the full screen, in GUI Forms' GRAY theme: a menu bar on the top
' -- row, the file name in the top edge of a box of double lines, 26 rows of 78 columns of text
' -- in the box, and a status row with F10=Menu, a message, the line and the column
' -- of the cursor. For the command line, not for scripts.
' -- F10 opens the File menu, and Alt with a menu's letter opens that menu. File: New, Open,
' -- Save, Save As, the recent files, Exit. The recent files are the last 4 opened or saved, as
' -- full paths of up to 60 characters, the last first; 1 to 4 opens one, after the save
' -- question. Edit: Cut, Copy, Paste, Clear. Search: Find, Repeat Last Find,
' -- Change. Options: Display. Help: DOS Help, About. A menu item does what its key does.
' -- Display chooses the colors, Gray, Dark or Light, and the tab stops, 8, 4, 3 or 2. OK
' -- writes C:\6502DOS.INI.
' -- New, Open and Exit first ask to save text with changes. New gives an empty text named
' -- UNTITLED. Open and Save As ask the file in the file dialog, its mask *.TXT. A file that
' -- does not open shows its error in a dialog and keeps the text; one that fails while it
' -- loads leaves an empty UNTITLED. Save As asks before it replaces a file. Save, Ctrl+S and
' -- the save question do Save As for UNTITLED.
' -- Ctrl+F asks the text to find in a dialog, with the check boxes Match Upper/Lowercase and
' -- Whole Word, then finds it. F3 finds the same text again. A find starts at the cursor,
' -- goes on from the text's start, selects the match and puts the cursor after it; with no
' -- match the status row shows Match not found. Ctrl+R asks the text to find and the text to
' -- put in its place, with the same check boxes; Change All changes every match in the text
' -- and shows the count on the status row.
' -- Left and Right move the cursor one character, Up and Down one line. Up and Down keep the
' -- column the cursor came from. Home and End go to the start and the end of the line. PgUp
' -- and PgDn move 26 lines. The view moves sideways 8 columns at a time to keep the cursor
' -- on screen. Ctrl+S saves the file. Ctrl+Q ends it, clears the screen and prints
' -- EDIT - The 6502DOS Editor... Bye!; text with changes first asks to save it in a dialog:
' -- Yes saves, No does not, and Esc goes back to the text.
' -- Shift+F1 asks the topic of DOS help in a dialog, with the word at the cursor, its letters
' -- and digits, filled in. OK shows the topic from C:\sys\HELP.HLP until a key is pressed, or
' -- with no topic the topic names. A topic not in HELP.HLP shows No help for TOPIC on the
' -- status row. A HELP.HLP that does not open shows its error on the status row.
' -- Ctrl+C is a key, not the STOP key. A save writes EDIT.$$$ in the file's directory, then
' -- gives it the file's name, so a failed save keeps the file as it was. With BAK=1 the old
' -- file is kept, renamed to the extension .BAK. Lines end in LF
' -- when the file's first line did, else in CR LF; a new file's lines end in CR LF.
' -- A typed character goes in at the cursor; there is no overwrite mode. Enter splits the
' -- line, Tab puts in a tab, Backspace takes out the character before the cursor and Delete
' -- the one under it; at a line's end they join two lines.
' -- Shift with a cursor key selects, from where the cursor was; the selection shows in
' -- reverse video. Another key but Ctrl+C ends it. Delete and Backspace take out the selection
' -- when there is one, and do not put it on the clipboard. Ctrl+C copies the selection to the
' -- clipboard, and Ctrl+X cuts it; with no selection they take the cursor's line and its line
' -- end. Ctrl+V puts the clipboard in at the cursor. The clipboard holds 2048 bytes; a larger
' -- selection shows Selection too large. The status row shows * before the line once
' -- the text has changed. Insufficient memory shows there when the text holds 65535 bytes or
' -- no RAM bank is free.
' -- A line ends at CR, LF or CR LF; the text keeps LF. A tab goes to the next column that is
' -- a multiple of the tab stop, 8 at the start. Another character below 32 shows as ".".
' -- The section [EDIT] of C:\6502DOS.INI changes the defaults, read at the start: THEME=DARK
' -- or LIGHT for the GRAY theme, TABS=2, 3 or 4 for 8, MATCHCASE=1 and WHOLEWORD=1 to check
' -- those boxes, FIND= the text to find, LINEENDS=LF for a new file's CR LF, and BAK=1 to
' -- keep the old file on a save. RECENT= holds the recent files, separated
' -- by |; EDIT writes it when they change.
' -- The text takes up to 8 RAM banks and holds 65535 bytes; the clipboard takes $9700 to $9EFF.
' -- A larger file prints File too large, and one with no RAM bank left Insufficient memory;
' -- both give exit code 2. A file that does not exist gives an empty text, and the
' -- status row says New file. No file name gives an empty UNTITLED. A second name prints
' -- Too many parameters and gives exit code 1. A file that does not open for
' -- another reason prints its error message and gives exit code 2. Exit code 0 otherwise.
' -- The console color at the start is put back at the end.
' --
' -- From a prompt:
' --     EDIT DOCS\README.TXT
' --     EDIT "MY NOTES.TXT"
'=============================================================================================
#INCLUDE "DOS.UXI"
#INCLUDE "HEAP.UXI"
#INCLUDE "KEYS.UXI"
#INCLUDE "CONS.UXI"
#INCLUDE "BANK.UXI"
#INCLUDE "VERA.UXI"
#INCLUDE "GUI.UXI"
#INCLUDE "PICKFILE.UXI"
CONST SLOT_P1 AS UBYTE = 0, SLOT_P2 AS UBYTE = 1

' The text shows on screen rows TEXT_TOP to TEXT_TOP + TEXT_ROWS - 1, from screen column
' LEFT_EDGE, COLUMNS wide, inside the box of the form EDIT_FORM. The status row is the
' screen's last; its right part starts at column STATUS_RIGHT.
CONST TEXT_TOP AS UBYTE = 2, TEXT_ROWS AS UBYTE = 26
CONST LEFT_EDGE AS UBYTE = 1, COLUMNS AS UBYTE = 78, STATUS_RIGHT AS UBYTE = 58
CONST SHIFT_STEP AS UBYTE = 8, NO_MARK AS UBYTE = 255
CONST CTRL_C AS UBYTE = 3, LF AS UBYTE = 10, CTRL_Q AS UBYTE = 17, CTRL_S AS UBYTE = 19
CONST CTRL_V AS UBYTE = 22, CTRL_X AS UBYTE = 24
CONST CTRL_F AS UBYTE = 6, CTRL_R AS UBYTE = 18, KEY_F3 AS UWORD = (KEYS.SCAN_F1 + 2) * 256
' SEARCH's answer when the text is not found. The fields of the Find and Change dialogs are
' FIND_WIDTH wide, after a caption of FIND_CAPTION columns and a space.
CONST NO_MATCH AS UWORD = $FFFF, FIND_WIDTH AS UBYTE = 30, FIND_CAPTION AS UBYTE = 10
CONST CLIPBOARD AS UWORD = $9700, CLIP_SIZE AS UWORD = 2048
' The text's banks show at WINDOW_START up to WINDOW_END. A buffer of MAX_BANKS banks holds
' MAX_ROOM bytes, the most a UWORD counts. MOVE_GAP and LOAD pass RUN_SIZE bytes at a time.
CONST WINDOW_START AS UWORD = $A000, WINDOW_END AS UWORD = $C000, BANK_SIZE AS UWORD = 8192
CONST MAX_BANKS AS UBYTE = 8, MAX_ROOM AS UWORD = 65535, RUN_SIZE AS UBYTE = 255
CONST DOS_HELP_NAME$ = "C:\sys\HELP.HLP"
' The menu items' ids. An item that a key does takes that key's code as its id; MENU_KEY turns
' the other ids into their keys.
CONST ID_CLEAR AS UBYTE = 200, ID_DOS_HELP AS UBYTE = 201, ID_ABOUT AS UBYTE = 202
CONST ID_FIND_AGAIN AS UBYTE = 203, ID_NEW AS UBYTE = 204, ID_OPEN AS UBYTE = 205
CONST ID_SAVE_AS AS UBYTE = 206, ID_DISPLAY AS UBYTE = 207
' The recent files are ID_RECENT to ID_RECENT + 3.
CONST ID_RECENT AS UBYTE = 208
' LOAD's answer for a file larger than MAX_ROOM.
CONST TOO_LARGE AS UBYTE = 254


DIM FILE_NAME AS STRING * 80, STATUS AS STRING * 120, MESSAGE AS STRING * 40
DIM EDITED_FILE AS UWORD
' NAMED is 0 for UNTITLED. PICKED gets the file dialog's path; KEPT holds FILE_NAME while a
' new name is tried.
DIM NAMED AS UBYTE, PICKED AS STRING * 80, KEPT AS STRING * 80
' The recent files, the last opened or saved first, as the File menu's captions: &1 to &4, a
' space and the full path in capitals; "" for none.
DIM RECENT_1 AS STRING * 63, RECENT_2 AS STRING * 63, RECENT_3 AS STRING * 63
DIM RECENT_4 AS STRING * 63
' The form that holds the box, the title and the menu bar, and the console color at the start.
DIM EDIT_FORM AS UBYTE, START_COLOR AS UBYTE
' The text is a gap buffer of ROOM bytes in BANK_COUNT RAM banks. Byte PLACE of the buffer is
' at WINDOW_START + PLACE MOD 8192 in bank PAGE_BANK(PLACE >> 8). Positions 0 to TEXT_LENGTH
' count the text's bytes. The bytes from GAP_POSITION on lie GAP_SIZE bytes further on.
DIM PAGE_BANK(256) AS UBYTE, BANK_COUNT AS UBYTE, ROOM AS UWORD
DIM TEXT_LENGTH AS UWORD, GAP_POSITION AS UWORD, GAP_SIZE AS UWORD
DIM RUN_BUFFER(RUN_SIZE) AS UBYTE
' CR_ENDS is 1 when the file's first line ends in CR. A save then writes each LF as CR LF,
' from CR_LF. A new file, or one with no line end, takes NEW_ENDS.
DIM CR_ENDS AS UBYTE, CR_LF(2) AS UBYTE, NEW_ENDS AS UBYTE
' A tab goes to the next column that is a multiple of TAB_SIZE.
' THEME_CHOICE is the theme, GRAY, DARK or LIGHT for 0 to 2. TAB_CHOICE is the tabs, 8, 4, 3
' or 2 columns for 0 to 3. BACKUP is 1 when a save keeps the old file as a .BAK.
DIM BACKUP AS UBYTE
DIM TAB_SIZE AS UBYTE, THEME_CHOICE AS UBYTE, TAB_CHOICE AS UBYTE
' LINE_BEGIN is where the cursor's line starts. GOAL is the column Up and Down aim for.
' NAVIGATING is 1 while an arrow, Home, End, PgUp or PgDn key is handled. PENDING is a key
' taken from the keyboard and not yet handled, or 0.
DIM CURSOR AS UWORD, CURSOR_LINE AS UWORD, LINE_BEGIN AS UWORD
DIM CURSOR_COLUMN AS UWORD, GOAL AS UWORD, VERTICAL AS UBYTE, NAVIGATING AS UBYTE
DIM PENDING AS UWORD
DIM TOP AS UWORD, TOP_LINE AS UWORD, LEFT_COLUMN AS UWORD
' NEED_SCREEN asks for the form, the menu bar and the page to be drawn again; NEED_PAGE for the
' page; NEED_ROW for line ROW_LINE, which starts at ROW_START.
DIM NEED_SCREEN AS UBYTE, NEED_PAGE AS UBYTE, NEED_ROW AS UBYTE
DIM ROW_LINE AS UWORD, ROW_START AS UWORD
DIM MODIFIED AS UBYTE
' The selection runs from ANCHOR to the cursor while SELECTING is 1. SHOW_ROW marks the
' positions SELECTION_BEGIN up to SELECTION_END; both are 0 with no selection.
DIM ANCHOR AS UWORD, SELECTING AS UBYTE, SELECTION_BEGIN AS UWORD, SELECTION_END AS UWORD
DIM NEW_BEGIN AS UWORD, NEW_END AS UWORD, OLD_LINE AS UWORD
DIM CLIP_LENGTH AS UWORD
DIM ROW_TEXT(COLUMNS) AS UBYTE
DIM KEY AS UWORD, MODIFIERS AS UBYTE, STEPS AS UBYTE, QUIT AS UBYTE
' The topic Shift+F1 asks for, as typed.
DIM TOPIC AS STRING * 20
' The Find and Change dialogs' fields and check boxes. FIND_LENGTH is the length of FIND_TEXT.
DIM FIND_TEXT AS STRING * 30, CHANGE_TEXT AS STRING * 30
DIM MATCH_CASE AS UBYTE, WHOLE_WORD AS UBYTE, FIND_LENGTH AS UBYTE




' Selects the bank of byte PLACE of the buffer, and returns the byte's address. Trap: the text
' routines run in the low part, as a region runs from the window the text's banks use.
FUNCT SELECT_PLACE(PLACE AS UWORD) AS UWORD
  DIM PAGE AS UBYTE
  PAGE = ContentsAt(@PLACE + 1)
  ContentsAt(BANK.RAM_BANK) = ContentsAt(@PAGE_BANK + PAGE)
  RETURN (PLACE AND (BANK_SIZE - 1)) OR WINDOW_START
END FUNCT



' The byte at position PLACE of the text. SELECT_PLACE's work is done here, for speed.
FUNCT BYTE_AT(PLACE AS UWORD) AS UBYTE
  DIM PAGE AS UBYTE
  IF PLACE >= GAP_POSITION THEN PLACE = PLACE + GAP_SIZE
  PAGE = ContentsAt(@PLACE + 1)
  ContentsAt(BANK.RAM_BANK) = ContentsAt(@PAGE_BANK + PAGE)
  RETURN ContentsAt((PLACE AND (BANK_SIZE - 1)) OR WINDOW_START)
END FUNCT



' Copies COUNT bytes between the buffer, from byte PLACE on, and low RAM, from ADDRESS on: into
' the buffer when INTO is 1, out of it when INTO is 0.
SUB TEXT_COPY(PLACE AS UWORD, ADDRESS AS UWORD, COUNT AS UWORD, INTO AS UBYTE)
  DIM WINDOW AS UWORD, RUN AS UWORD, SOURCE AS UWORD, TARGET AS UWORD
  DO WHILE COUNT > 0
    WINDOW = SELECT_PLACE(PLACE)
    RUN = WINDOW_END - WINDOW
    IF RUN > COUNT THEN RUN = COUNT
    PLACE = PLACE + RUN
    COUNT = COUNT - RUN
    SOURCE = WINDOW
    TARGET = ADDRESS
    IF INTO = 1 THEN
      SOURCE = ADDRESS
      TARGET = WINDOW
    END IF
    ADDRESS = ADDRESS + RUN
    ' Copies RUN bytes from SOURCE to TARGET: the whole pages, then the rest. $22 and $24 are
    ' the runtime's ZP_PTR and ZP_TMP, free between statements.
    ASM
        lda @SOURCE
        sta $22
        lda @SOURCE + 1
        sta $23
        lda @TARGET
        sta $24
        lda @TARGET + 1
        sta $25
        phx
        ldy #0
        ldx @RUN + 1
        beq part
page:   lda ($22),y
        sta ($24),y
        iny
        bne page
        inc $23
        inc $25
        dex
        bne page
part:   ldx @RUN
        beq done
rest:   lda ($22),y
        sta ($24),y
        iny
        dex
        bne rest
done:   plx
    END ASM
  LOOP
END SUB



' Moves the gap to position PLACE. The bytes pass through RUN_BUFFER, as the bank they come
' from and the bank they go to may differ.
SUB MOVE_GAP(PLACE AS UWORD)
  DIM COUNT AS UWORD
  IF GAP_SIZE = 0 THEN GAP_POSITION = PLACE
  DO WHILE GAP_POSITION > PLACE
    COUNT = GAP_POSITION - PLACE
    IF COUNT > RUN_SIZE THEN COUNT = RUN_SIZE
    GAP_POSITION = GAP_POSITION - COUNT
    TEXT_COPY(GAP_POSITION, @RUN_BUFFER, COUNT, 0)
    TEXT_COPY(GAP_POSITION + GAP_SIZE, @RUN_BUFFER, COUNT, 1)
  LOOP
  DO WHILE GAP_POSITION < PLACE
    COUNT = PLACE - GAP_POSITION
    IF COUNT > RUN_SIZE THEN COUNT = RUN_SIZE
    TEXT_COPY(GAP_POSITION + GAP_SIZE, @RUN_BUFFER, COUNT, 0)
    TEXT_COPY(GAP_POSITION, @RUN_BUFFER, COUNT, 1)
    GAP_POSITION = GAP_POSITION + COUNT
  LOOP
END SUB



' Takes one more RAM bank for the buffer, and puts the gap at the text's end, so the gap grows
' by the bank. Returns 1, or 0 when MAX_BANKS are taken or no bank is free.
FUNCT GROW() AS UBYTE
  DIM NUMBER AS UBYTE, PAGE AS UBYTE, ADDED AS UWORD
  IF BANK_COUNT = MAX_BANKS THEN RETURN 0
  NUMBER = BANK.ALLOC(1)
  IF NUMBER = 0 THEN RETURN 0
  MOVE_GAP(TEXT_LENGTH)
  ' The bank's 32 pages of PAGE_BANK; PAGE wraps to 0 after the eighth bank's.
  PAGE = BANK_COUNT * 32
  DO
    PAGE_BANK(PAGE) = NUMBER
    PAGE = PAGE + 1
  LOOP UNTIL (PAGE AND 31) = 0
  BANK_COUNT = BANK_COUNT + 1
  ADDED = BANK_SIZE
  IF BANK_COUNT = MAX_BANKS THEN ADDED = BANK_SIZE - 1
  ROOM = ROOM + ADDED
  GAP_SIZE = GAP_SIZE + ADDED
  RETURN 1
END FUNCT



' Grows the buffer until the gap holds NEEDED bytes. Returns 1, or 0 when it cannot.
FUNCT MAKE_ROOM(NEEDED AS UWORD) AS UBYTE
  DO WHILE GAP_SIZE < NEEDED
    IF GROW() = 0 THEN RETURN 0
  LOOP
  RETURN 1
END FUNCT



' Asks for the cursor's row to be drawn again. A row already asked for on another line gives
' the whole page, since the edit may have moved where that line starts.
SUB CHANGED_ROW()
  IF NEED_ROW = 1 AND ROW_LINE <> CURSOR_LINE THEN NEED_PAGE = 1
  NEED_ROW = 1
  ROW_LINE = CURSOR_LINE
  ROW_START = LINE_BEGIN
END SUB



' Puts CHARACTER into the text at the cursor and moves the cursor past it. LF starts a new
' line. A full buffer that cannot grow sets MESSAGE instead.
SUB INSERT(CHARACTER AS UBYTE)
  IF MAKE_ROOM(1) = 0 THEN
    MESSAGE = "Insufficient memory"
  ELSE
    MOVE_GAP(CURSOR)
    ContentsAt(SELECT_PLACE(GAP_POSITION)) = CHARACTER
    GAP_POSITION = GAP_POSITION + 1
    GAP_SIZE = GAP_SIZE - 1
    TEXT_LENGTH = TEXT_LENGTH + 1
    CURSOR = CURSOR + 1
    MODIFIED = 1
    IF CHARACTER = LF THEN
      LINE_BEGIN = CURSOR
      CURSOR_LINE = CURSOR_LINE + 1
      NEED_PAGE = 1
    ELSE
      CHANGED_ROW()
    END IF
  END IF
END SUB



' Takes the byte at position PLACE out of the text.
SUB REMOVE(PLACE AS UWORD)
  MOVE_GAP(PLACE)
  GAP_SIZE = GAP_SIZE + 1
  TEXT_LENGTH = TEXT_LENGTH - 1
  MODIFIED = 1
END SUB



' Where the line that holds position PLACE starts.
FUNCT LINE_START(PLACE AS UWORD) AS UWORD
  DO WHILE PLACE > 0
    IF BYTE_AT(PLACE - 1) = LF THEN EXIT DO
    PLACE = PLACE - 1
  LOOP
  RETURN PLACE
END FUNCT



' Where the line that holds position PLACE ends: its LF, or TEXT_LENGTH.
FUNCT LINE_END(PLACE AS UWORD) AS UWORD
  DO WHILE PLACE < TEXT_LENGTH
    IF BYTE_AT(PLACE) = LF THEN EXIT DO
    PLACE = PLACE + 1
  LOOP
  RETURN PLACE
END FUNCT



' The screen column after CHARACTER, shown at column COLUMN.
FUNCT NEXT_COLUMN(CHARACTER AS UBYTE, COLUMN AS UWORD) AS UWORD
  IF CHARACTER = KEYS.TAB THEN RETURN COLUMN + TAB_SIZE - COLUMN MOD TAB_SIZE
  RETURN COLUMN + 1
END FUNCT




' The screen column of position PLACE on the line that starts at START.
FUNCT COLUMN_OF(START AS UWORD, PLACE AS UWORD) AS UWORD
  DIM COLUMN AS UWORD
  COLUMN = 0
  DO WHILE START < PLACE
    COLUMN = NEXT_COLUMN(BYTE_AT(START), COLUMN)
    START = START + 1
  LOOP
  RETURN COLUMN
END FUNCT




' The position on the line that starts at START nearest to screen column GOAL, not past it.
FUNCT POSITION_AT(START AS UWORD, GOAL AS UWORD) AS UWORD
  DIM COLUMN AS UWORD, CHARACTER AS UBYTE
  COLUMN = 0
  DO WHILE START < TEXT_LENGTH
    CHARACTER = BYTE_AT(START)
    IF CHARACTER = LF THEN EXIT DO
    COLUMN = NEXT_COLUMN(CHARACTER, COLUMN)
    IF COLUMN > GOAL THEN EXIT DO
    START = START + 1
  LOOP
  RETURN START
END FUNCT



' Moves LINE_BEGIN and CURSOR_LINE to the line below. Returns 1, or 0 on the last line.
FUNCT LINE_DOWN() AS UBYTE
  DIM FINISH AS UWORD
  FINISH = LINE_END(LINE_BEGIN)
  IF FINISH >= TEXT_LENGTH THEN RETURN 0
  LINE_BEGIN = FINISH + 1
  CURSOR_LINE = CURSOR_LINE + 1
  RETURN 1
END FUNCT



' Moves LINE_BEGIN and CURSOR_LINE to the line above. Returns 1, or 0 on the first line.
FUNCT LINE_UP() AS UBYTE
  IF LINE_BEGIN = 0 THEN RETURN 0
  LINE_BEGIN = LINE_START(LINE_BEGIN - 1)
  CURSOR_LINE = CURSOR_LINE - 1
  RETURN 1
END FUNCT



' Takes positions BEGIN up to FINISH out of the text and puts the cursor at BEGIN. The cursor
' must be at BEGIN or FINISH, or between them on one line.
SUB REMOVE_PART(BEGIN AS UWORD, FINISH AS UWORD)
  DIM PLACE AS UWORD
  MOVE_GAP(FINISH)
  IF CURSOR = FINISH THEN
    PLACE = BEGIN
    DO WHILE PLACE < FINISH
      IF BYTE_AT(PLACE) = LF THEN CURSOR_LINE = CURSOR_LINE - 1
      PLACE = PLACE + 1
    LOOP
  END IF
  ' The part lies just before the gap, so the gap takes it in.
  GAP_POSITION = BEGIN
  GAP_SIZE = GAP_SIZE + FINISH - BEGIN
  TEXT_LENGTH = TEXT_LENGTH - (FINISH - BEGIN)
  CURSOR = BEGIN
  LINE_BEGIN = LINE_START(BEGIN)
  MODIFIED = 1
  NEED_PAGE = 1
END SUB



' Puts the selection on the clipboard, or the cursor's line and its line end when there is
' none. CUT = 1 also takes it out of the text. A part over CLIP_SIZE bytes sets MESSAGE
' instead.
SUB TAKE(CUT AS UBYTE)
  DIM BEGIN AS UWORD, FINISH AS UWORD
  BEGIN = SELECTION_BEGIN
  FINISH = SELECTION_END
  IF FINISH = BEGIN THEN
    BEGIN = LINE_BEGIN
    FINISH = LINE_END(BEGIN)
    IF FINISH < TEXT_LENGTH THEN FINISH = FINISH + 1
  END IF
  IF FINISH - BEGIN > CLIP_SIZE THEN
    MESSAGE = "Selection too large"
    RETURN
  END IF
  MOVE_GAP(FINISH)
  CLIP_LENGTH = FINISH - BEGIN
  TEXT_COPY(BEGIN, CLIPBOARD, CLIP_LENGTH, 0)
  IF CUT = 1 AND CLIP_LENGTH > 0 THEN REMOVE_PART(BEGIN, FINISH)
END SUB



' Puts the clipboard into the text at the cursor and moves the cursor past it. A full buffer
' that cannot grow sets MESSAGE instead.
SUB PASTE()
  DIM LINES AS UWORD, PLACE AS UWORD
  IF MAKE_ROOM(CLIP_LENGTH) = 0 THEN
    MESSAGE = "Insufficient memory"
    RETURN
  END IF
  IF CLIP_LENGTH = 0 THEN RETURN
  MOVE_GAP(CURSOR)
  TEXT_COPY(GAP_POSITION, CLIPBOARD, CLIP_LENGTH, 1)
  LINES = 0
  PLACE = CLIPBOARD
  DO WHILE PLACE < CLIPBOARD + CLIP_LENGTH
    IF ContentsAt(PLACE) = LF THEN LINES = LINES + 1
    PLACE = PLACE + 1
  LOOP
  GAP_POSITION = GAP_POSITION + CLIP_LENGTH
  GAP_SIZE = GAP_SIZE - CLIP_LENGTH
  TEXT_LENGTH = TEXT_LENGTH + CLIP_LENGTH
  CURSOR = CURSOR + CLIP_LENGTH
  MODIFIED = 1
  IF LINES = 0 THEN
    CHANGED_ROW()
  ELSE
    CURSOR_LINE = CURSOR_LINE + LINES
    LINE_BEGIN = LINE_START(CURSOR)
    NEED_PAGE = 1
  END IF
END SUB




' Writes ROW_TEXT from index FIRST up to LAST.
SUB PUT_RUN(FIRST AS UBYTE, LAST AS UBYTE)
  IF LAST > FIRST THEN WRITE 1, @ROW_TEXT + FIRST, LAST - FIRST
END SUB



' Shows the line that starts at START on text row ROW, from column LEFT_COLUMN, and blanks
' the rest of the row up to the box's right edge. The selected part shows in reverse video, a
' selected line end as one space. START past TEXT_LENGTH gives a blank row. Returns where the
' next line starts, past TEXT_LENGTH when none does.
FUNCT SHOW_ROW(ROW AS UBYTE, START AS UWORD) AS UWORD
  DIM COLUMN AS UWORD, LAST AS UWORD, COUNT AS UBYTE, CHARACTER AS UBYTE
  DIM MARKED AS UBYTE, MARK_FROM AS UBYTE, MARK_TO AS UBYTE, TAB_END AS UWORD
  POS(1) = ROW + TEXT_TOP
  POS(0) = LEFT_EDGE
  COUNT = 0
  ' ROW_TEXT is marked from MARK_FROM up to MARK_TO.
  MARK_FROM = NO_MARK
  MARK_TO = 0
  IF START <= TEXT_LENGTH THEN
    COLUMN = 0
    LAST = LEFT_COLUMN + COLUMNS
    CHARACTER = 0
    DO WHILE START < TEXT_LENGTH
      CHARACTER = BYTE_AT(START)
      MARKED = 0
      IF START >= SELECTION_BEGIN AND START < SELECTION_END THEN
        MARKED = 1
        IF MARK_FROM = NO_MARK THEN MARK_FROM = COUNT
      END IF
      START = START + 1
      IF CHARACTER = LF THEN
        IF MARKED = 1 AND COLUMN >= LEFT_COLUMN AND COLUMN < LAST THEN
          ROW_TEXT(COUNT) = KEYS.SPACE
          COUNT = COUNT + 1
          MARK_TO = COUNT
        END IF
        EXIT DO
      END IF
      IF CHARACTER = KEYS.TAB THEN
        TAB_END = NEXT_COLUMN(KEYS.TAB, COLUMN)
        DO
          IF COLUMN >= LEFT_COLUMN AND COLUMN < LAST THEN
            ROW_TEXT(COUNT) = KEYS.SPACE
            COUNT = COUNT + 1
          END IF
          COLUMN = COLUMN + 1
        LOOP UNTIL COLUMN = TAB_END
      ELSE
        IF COLUMN >= LEFT_COLUMN AND COLUMN < LAST THEN
          IF CHARACTER < KEYS.SPACE THEN CHARACTER = ASC(".")
          ROW_TEXT(COUNT) = CHARACTER
          COUNT = COUNT + 1
        END IF
        COLUMN = COLUMN + 1
      END IF
      IF MARKED = 1 THEN MARK_TO = COUNT
    LOOP
    IF CHARACTER <> LF THEN START = TEXT_LENGTH + 1
  END IF
  IF MARK_FROM = NO_MARK THEN
    MARK_FROM = COUNT
    MARK_TO = COUNT
  END IF
  PUT_RUN(0, MARK_FROM)
  IF MARK_TO > MARK_FROM THEN
    PRINT CONS.REVERSE$;
    PUT_RUN(MARK_FROM, MARK_TO)
    PRINT CONS.NORMAL$;
  END IF
  ' Spaces, not CLEAR_EOL$, blank the rest, which would take the box's right edge too.
  DO WHILE COUNT < COLUMNS
    ROW_TEXT(COUNT) = KEYS.SPACE
    COUNT = COUNT + 1
  LOOP
  PUT_RUN(MARK_TO, COUNT)
  RETURN START
END FUNCT



' Shows the page from line TOP.
SUB SHOW_PAGE()
  DIM ROW AS UBYTE, START AS UWORD
  START = TOP
  FOR ROW = 0 TO TEXT_ROWS - 1
    START = SHOW_ROW(ROW, START)
  NEXT
END SUB



' Shows the status row: F10=Menu and MESSAGE at the left; at STATUS_RIGHT a * when the
' text has changed, the line and the column. The right part ends before the screen's last
' column, so the screen does not scroll.
SUB SHOW_STATUS()
  GUI.STATUS_LINE(LEFT$(" F10=Menu  " + MESSAGE, STATUS_RIGHT - 1))
  IF MODIFIED = 1 THEN
    STATUS = "*"
  ELSE
    STATUS = " "
  END IF
  STATUS = STATUS + " Ln" + STR$(CURSOR_LINE + 1) + "  Col" + STR$(CURSOR_COLUMN + 1)
  POS(0) = STATUS_RIGHT
  PRINT STATUS;
END SUB



' Shows the topic TOPIC of DOS_HELP_NAME$ on a clear screen
' until a key is pressed, then asks for the page. In the file a line :HEADING starts the topic
' HEADING, in capitals, up to the next such line. With no topic the lines before the first
' heading show, then the headings. A TOPIC not in the file sets MESSAGE to No help for TOPIC
' and leaves the screen uncleared.
' Each LF goes out after a CR, since the console's LF keeps the column. A file that does not
' open sets MESSAGE to its error.
SUB SHOW_TEXT()
  DIM HELP_FILE AS UWORD, COUNT AS UWORD, PLACE AS UWORD, CHARACTER AS UBYTE
  DIM AT_LINE_START AS UBYTE, IN_HEADING AS UBYTE, SHOWING AS UBYTE, MATCHING AS UBYTE
  DIM LETTER AS UBYTE, TOPIC_LENGTH AS UBYTE, TOPIC_LETTER AS UBYTE
  HELP_FILE = DOS.OPEN_FILE(DOS_HELP_NAME$, DOS.ACCESS_READ)
  TOPIC_LENGTH = LEN(TOPIC)
  IF HELP_FILE = NOFILE THEN
    MESSAGE = DOS.ERRMSG(DOS.ERROR)
    RETURN
  END IF
  SHOWING = 0
  IF TOPIC_LENGTH = 0 THEN
    SHOWING = 1
    GUI.USE_COLOR(GUI.ROLE.TEXT)
    PRINT CONS.CLEAR_SCREEN$;
    CONS.LOCATE(2, 0)
  END IF
  IN_HEADING = 0
  AT_LINE_START = 1
  DO
    COUNT = DOS.READ_FILE(HELP_FILE, @ROW_TEXT, COLUMNS)
    PLACE = 0
    DO WHILE PLACE < COUNT
      CHARACTER = ROW_TEXT(PLACE)
      PLACE = PLACE + 1
      IF AT_LINE_START = 1 AND CHARACTER = ASC(":") THEN
        IF SHOWING = 1 AND TOPIC_LENGTH <> 0 THEN
          COUNT = 0
          EXIT DO
        END IF
        SHOWING = 0
        IN_HEADING = 1
        MATCHING = 1
        LETTER = 0
      ELSEIF IN_HEADING = 1 THEN
        IF CHARACTER = LF THEN
          IN_HEADING = 0
          IF LETTER = TOPIC_LENGTH AND MATCHING = 1 THEN
            SHOWING = 1
            GUI.USE_COLOR(GUI.ROLE.TEXT)
            PRINT CONS.CLEAR_SCREEN$;
            CONS.LOCATE(2, 0)
          END IF
          IF TOPIC_LENGTH = 0 THEN PRINT " ";
        ELSE
          IF TOPIC_LENGTH = 0 THEN
            DOS.REG_A = CHARACTER
            SYS DOS.API_CON_OUT
          END IF
          TOPIC_LETTER = ContentsAt(@TOPIC + 2 + LETTER)
          IF TOPIC_LETTER >= ASC("a") THEN TOPIC_LETTER = TOPIC_LETTER - 32
          IF LETTER >= TOPIC_LENGTH OR TOPIC_LETTER <> CHARACTER THEN MATCHING = 0
          LETTER = LETTER + 1
        END IF
      ELSEIF SHOWING = 1 THEN
        IF CHARACTER = LF THEN
          DOS.REG_A = KEYS.ENTER
          SYS DOS.API_CON_OUT
        END IF
        DOS.REG_A = CHARACTER
        SYS DOS.API_CON_OUT
      END IF
      AT_LINE_START = CHARACTER = LF
    LOOP
  LOOP UNTIL COUNT < COLUMNS
  DOS.CLOSE_FILE(HELP_FILE)
  NEED_SCREEN = 1
  IF SHOWING = 0 AND TOPIC_LENGTH <> 0 THEN
    MESSAGE = "No help for " + TOPIC
    RETURN
  END IF
  KEY = WAITKEY()
END SUB



' 1 when CHARACTER is a letter or a digit.
FUNCT IS_WORD(CHARACTER AS UBYTE) AS UBYTE
  IF CHARACTER >= ASC("a") THEN CHARACTER = CHARACTER - 32
  IF CHARACTER >= ASC("A") AND CHARACTER <= ASC("Z") THEN RETURN 1
  RETURN CHARACTER >= ASC("0") AND CHARACTER <= ASC("9")
END FUNCT



' Asks the topic of DOS help in a dialog, with the word at the cursor, then shows that topic
' of DOS_HELP_NAME$ after OK.
SUB SHOW_DOS_HELP()
  DIM START AS UWORD, FINISH AS UWORD
  START = CURSOR
  DO WHILE START > 0
    IF IS_WORD(BYTE_AT(START - 1)) = 0 THEN EXIT DO
    START = START - 1
  LOOP
  FINISH = CURSOR
  DO WHILE FINISH < TEXT_LENGTH
    IF IS_WORD(BYTE_AT(FINISH)) = 0 THEN EXIT DO
    FINISH = FINISH + 1
  LOOP
  IF FINISH - START > 19 THEN FINISH = START + 19
  TOPIC = ""
  DO WHILE START < FINISH
    TOPIC = TOPIC + CHR$(BYTE_AT(START))
    START = START + 1
  LOOP
  IF GUI.INPUTBOX("DOS Help", "Topic, or none for the list:", TOPIC, 20) = 1 THEN SHOW_TEXT()
END SUB



' CHARACTER in capitals when it is a small letter, else CHARACTER.
FUNCT CAPITAL(CHARACTER AS UBYTE) AS UBYTE
  IF CHARACTER >= ASC("a") AND CHARACTER <= ASC("z") THEN RETURN CHARACTER - 32
  RETURN CHARACTER
END FUNCT



' 1 when FIND_TEXT is in the text at position PLACE. With MATCH_CASE = 0 a letter matches in
' either case. With WHOLE_WORD = 1 no letter or digit touches the match on either side.
FUNCT MATCH_AT(PLACE AS UWORD) AS UBYTE
  DIM INDEX AS UBYTE, FOUND AS UBYTE, WANTED AS UBYTE
  IF PLACE + FIND_LENGTH > TEXT_LENGTH THEN RETURN 0
  INDEX = 0
  DO WHILE INDEX < FIND_LENGTH
    FOUND = BYTE_AT(PLACE + INDEX)
    WANTED = ContentsAt(@FIND_TEXT + 2 + INDEX)
    IF MATCH_CASE = 0 THEN
      FOUND = CAPITAL(FOUND)
      WANTED = CAPITAL(WANTED)
    END IF
    IF FOUND <> WANTED THEN RETURN 0
    INDEX = INDEX + 1
  LOOP
  IF WHOLE_WORD = 1 THEN
    IF PLACE > 0 THEN
      IF IS_WORD(BYTE_AT(PLACE - 1)) = 1 THEN RETURN 0
    END IF
    PLACE = PLACE + FIND_LENGTH
    IF PLACE < TEXT_LENGTH THEN
      IF IS_WORD(BYTE_AT(PLACE)) = 1 THEN RETURN 0
    END IF
  END IF
  RETURN 1
END FUNCT



' The first position from FROM up to LIMIT where FIND_TEXT is, or NO_MATCH. Only a position
' whose byte equals FIND_TEXT's first byte with bit 5 set in both goes to MATCH_AT.
FUNCT SEARCH(FROM AS UWORD, LIMIT AS UWORD) AS UWORD
  DIM FIRST AS UBYTE
  FIRST = ContentsAt(@FIND_TEXT + 2) OR 32
  DO WHILE FROM < LIMIT
    IF (BYTE_AT(FROM) OR 32) = FIRST THEN
      IF MATCH_AT(FROM) = 1 THEN RETURN FROM
    END IF
    FROM = FROM + 1
  LOOP
  RETURN NO_MATCH
END FUNCT



' Where line NUMBER starts; the first line is 0.
FUNCT LINE_AT(NUMBER AS UWORD) AS UWORD
  DIM PLACE AS UWORD
  PLACE = 0
  DO WHILE NUMBER > 0
    PLACE = LINE_END(PLACE) + 1
    NUMBER = NUMBER - 1
  LOOP
  RETURN PLACE
END FUNCT



' Moves the cursor to position PLACE, and LINE_BEGIN and CURSOR_LINE with it.
SUB GO_TO(PLACE AS UWORD)
  IF PLACE < LINE_BEGIN THEN
    LINE_BEGIN = 0
    CURSOR_LINE = 0
  END IF
  DO WHILE LINE_END(LINE_BEGIN) < PLACE
    LINE_DOWN()
  LOOP
  CURSOR = PLACE
END SUB



' Finds FIND_TEXT from the cursor to the end of the text, then from the start. Selects the
' match and puts the cursor after it, or sets MESSAGE to Match not found. An empty FIND_TEXT
' does nothing.
SUB FIND_AGAIN()
  DIM PLACE AS UWORD
  FIND_LENGTH = LEN(FIND_TEXT)
  IF FIND_LENGTH = 0 THEN RETURN
  PLACE = SEARCH(CURSOR, TEXT_LENGTH)
  IF PLACE = NO_MATCH THEN PLACE = SEARCH(0, CURSOR)
  IF PLACE = NO_MATCH THEN
    MESSAGE = "Match not found"
    RETURN
  END IF
  GO_TO(PLACE + FIND_LENGTH)
  ANCHOR = PLACE
  SELECTING = 1
END SUB



' Changes each FIND_TEXT in the text to CHANGE_TEXT, from the start, and sets MESSAGE to the
' count changed, or to Match not found. The cursor keeps its line, and its column as near as
' the line allows; the page keeps its top line. A full buffer that cannot grow stops it, with
' Insufficient memory.
' An empty FIND_TEXT does nothing.
SUB CHANGE_ALL()
  DIM PLACE AS UWORD, COUNT AS UWORD, CHANGE_LENGTH AS UBYTE
  FIND_LENGTH = LEN(FIND_TEXT)
  IF FIND_LENGTH = 0 THEN RETURN
  CHANGE_LENGTH = LEN(CHANGE_TEXT)
  COUNT = 0
  PLACE = 0
  DO
    PLACE = SEARCH(PLACE, TEXT_LENGTH)
    IF PLACE = NO_MATCH THEN EXIT DO
    IF CHANGE_LENGTH > FIND_LENGTH THEN
      IF MAKE_ROOM(CHANGE_LENGTH - FIND_LENGTH) = 0 THEN
        MESSAGE = "Insufficient memory"
        EXIT DO
      END IF
    END IF
    ' The match lies just before the gap, so the gap takes it in; CHANGE_TEXT then fills the
    ' gap's start.
    MOVE_GAP(PLACE + FIND_LENGTH)
    GAP_POSITION = PLACE
    GAP_SIZE = GAP_SIZE + FIND_LENGTH - CHANGE_LENGTH
    TEXT_LENGTH = TEXT_LENGTH - FIND_LENGTH + CHANGE_LENGTH
    TEXT_COPY(GAP_POSITION, @CHANGE_TEXT + 2, CHANGE_LENGTH, 1)
    GAP_POSITION = GAP_POSITION + CHANGE_LENGTH
    PLACE = GAP_POSITION
    COUNT = COUNT + 1
  LOOP
  IF COUNT = 0 THEN
    IF MESSAGE = "" THEN MESSAGE = "Match not found"
    RETURN
  END IF
  IF MESSAGE = "" THEN MESSAGE = STR$(COUNT) + " changed"
  MODIFIED = 1
  ' The fields hold no line end, so the lines keep their numbers.
  TOP = LINE_AT(TOP_LINE)
  LINE_BEGIN = LINE_AT(CURSOR_LINE)
  CURSOR = POSITION_AT(LINE_BEGIN, CURSOR_COLUMN)
  NEED_PAGE = 1
END SUB




' Sets CURSOR_COLUMN, and moves the page and the view sideways so the cursor shows. Asks for
' the page to be drawn again when it moved.
SUB FOLLOW_CURSOR()
  CURSOR_COLUMN = COLUMN_OF(LINE_BEGIN, CURSOR)
  IF VERTICAL = 0 THEN GOAL = CURSOR_COLUMN
  IF CURSOR_LINE < TOP_LINE THEN
    TOP = LINE_BEGIN
    TOP_LINE = CURSOR_LINE
    NEED_PAGE = 1
  END IF
  IF CURSOR_LINE >= TOP_LINE + TEXT_ROWS THEN
    NEED_PAGE = 1
    DO WHILE CURSOR_LINE >= TOP_LINE + TEXT_ROWS
      TOP = LINE_END(TOP) + 1
      TOP_LINE = TOP_LINE + 1
    LOOP
  END IF
  IF CURSOR_COLUMN < LEFT_COLUMN THEN
    LEFT_COLUMN = CURSOR_COLUMN - (CURSOR_COLUMN AND (SHIFT_STEP - 1))
    NEED_PAGE = 1
  END IF
  IF CURSOR_COLUMN >= LEFT_COLUMN + COLUMNS THEN
    LEFT_COLUMN = CURSOR_COLUMN - COLUMNS + SHIFT_STEP
    LEFT_COLUMN = LEFT_COLUMN - (LEFT_COLUMN AND (SHIFT_STEP - 1))
    NEED_PAGE = 1
  END IF
END SUB




' Draws what FOLLOW_CURSOR, the edits, the menus and the dialogs asked for and the status row,
' and puts the cursor in place and shows it. A menu or a dialog with no room on VERA.UXI's
' stack sets GUI.SHOWN_FORM to 0, which asks for the screen too.
SUB DRAW()
  IF GUI.SHOWN_FORM <> EDIT_FORM THEN NEED_SCREEN = 1
  IF NEED_SCREEN = 1 THEN
    GUI.DRAW_WHOLE(EDIT_FORM)
    NEED_PAGE = 1
  END IF
  GUI.USE_COLOR(GUI.ROLE.TEXT)
  IF NEED_PAGE = 1 THEN
    SHOW_PAGE()
  ELSEIF NEED_ROW = 1 THEN
    IF ROW_LINE >= TOP_LINE AND ROW_LINE < TOP_LINE + TEXT_ROWS THEN
      SHOW_ROW(ROW_LINE - TOP_LINE, ROW_START)
    END IF
  END IF
  NEED_SCREEN = 0
  NEED_PAGE = 0
  NEED_ROW = 0
  SHOW_STATUS()
  CONS.LOCATE(CURSOR_LINE - TOP_LINE + TEXT_TOP, CURSOR_COLUMN - LEFT_COLUMN + LEFT_EDGE)
  CURSOR ON
END SUB




' Loads the file FILE_NAME into the buffer as the text, its CR LF and CR turned into LF, with
' the gap after it. Returns 0, or an error number, or TOO_LARGE. A file that does not open
' keeps the text, and leaves EDITED_FILE NOFILE. A file that fails after it opened leaves part
' of the text.
FUNCT LOAD() AS UBYTE
  DIM LOADED AS UBYTE, READ_PLACE AS UBYTE, COUNT AS UBYTE, CHARACTER AS UBYTE
  DIM SEEN AS UBYTE, AFTER_CR AS UBYTE, CODE AS UBYTE
  EDITED_FILE = DOS.OPEN_FILE(FILE_NAME, DOS.ACCESS_READ)
  IF EDITED_FILE = NOFILE THEN RETURN DOS.ERROR
  CR_ENDS = NEW_ENDS
  TEXT_LENGTH = 0
  GAP_POSITION = 0
  GAP_SIZE = ROOM
  SEEN = 0
  ' AFTER_CR is 1 after a CR, so an LF that follows it, in this run or the next, is dropped.
  AFTER_CR = 0
  DO
    LOADED = DOS.READ_FILE(EDITED_FILE, @RUN_BUFFER, RUN_SIZE)
    CODE = DOS.ERROR
    IF CODE <> 0 OR LOADED = 0 THEN EXIT DO
    ' The run's line ends are turned into LF in RUN_BUFFER, COUNT bytes kept.
    READ_PLACE = 0
    COUNT = 0
    DO WHILE READ_PLACE < LOADED
      CHARACTER = RUN_BUFFER(READ_PLACE)
      READ_PLACE = READ_PLACE + 1
      IF CHARACTER = LF AND AFTER_CR = 1 THEN
        AFTER_CR = 0
        CONTINUE
      END IF
      AFTER_CR = 0
      IF CHARACTER = KEYS.ENTER THEN
        SEEN = 1
        CHARACTER = LF
        AFTER_CR = 1
      ELSEIF CHARACTER = LF THEN
        IF SEEN = 0 THEN CR_ENDS = 0
        SEEN = 1
      END IF
      RUN_BUFFER(COUNT) = CHARACTER
      COUNT = COUNT + 1
    LOOP
    IF COUNT > MAX_ROOM - TEXT_LENGTH THEN
      CODE = TOO_LARGE
      EXIT DO
    END IF
    IF MAKE_ROOM(COUNT) = 0 THEN
      CODE = DOS.ERR_NO_MEMORY
      EXIT DO
    END IF
    TEXT_COPY(GAP_POSITION, @RUN_BUFFER, COUNT, 1)
    GAP_POSITION = GAP_POSITION + COUNT
    GAP_SIZE = GAP_SIZE - COUNT
    TEXT_LENGTH = TEXT_LENGTH + COUNT
  LOOP
  DOS.CLOSE_FILE(EDITED_FILE)
  RETURN CODE
END FUNCT



' Writes COUNT bytes of the buffer, from byte PLACE on, to EDITED_FILE, each LF as CR LF when
' CR_ENDS is 1. Returns 0, an error number, or DOS.DISK_FULL when the file took fewer bytes.
FUNCT WRITE_PART(PLACE AS UWORD, COUNT AS UWORD) AS UBYTE
  DIM ADDRESS AS UWORD, RUN AS UWORD, LIMIT AS UWORD
  DO WHILE COUNT > 0
    ' A write stays in one bank.
    ADDRESS = SELECT_PLACE(PLACE)
    LIMIT = WINDOW_END - ADDRESS
    IF LIMIT > COUNT THEN LIMIT = COUNT
    RUN = LIMIT
    IF CR_ENDS = 1 THEN
      RUN = 0
      DO WHILE RUN < LIMIT
        IF ContentsAt(ADDRESS + RUN) = LF THEN EXIT DO
        RUN = RUN + 1
      LOOP
    END IF
    IF RUN > 0 THEN
      IF DOS.WRITE_FILE(EDITED_FILE, ADDRESS, RUN) < RUN THEN EXIT DO
      PLACE = PLACE + RUN
      COUNT = COUNT - RUN
    ELSE
      IF DOS.WRITE_FILE(EDITED_FILE, @CR_LF, 2) < 2 THEN EXIT DO
      PLACE = PLACE + 1
      COUNT = COUNT - 1
    END IF
  LOOP
  IF COUNT = 0 THEN RETURN 0
  IF DOS.ERROR <> 0 THEN RETURN DOS.ERROR
  RETURN DOS.DISK_FULL
END FUNCT



' Saves the text to FILE_NAME. It is written to EDIT.$$$ in the file's directory, then
' CLEAR_OLD moves the file out of the way and EDIT.$$$ takes its name. A failed write keeps the file as it was.
' Sets MESSAGE to Saved and clears MODIFIED, or sets MESSAGE to the error. Returns 0 or the
' error number.
FUNCT SAVE() AS UBYTE
  DIM TEMPORARY AS STRING * 90, LENGTH AS UBYTE, PLACE AS UBYTE, CODE AS UBYTE
  ' LENGTH ends as the length of the directory part: up to the last \, / or :.
  LENGTH = 0
  FOR PLACE = 1 TO LEN(FILE_NAME)
    SELECT CASE ContentsAt(@FILE_NAME + 1 + PLACE)
      CASE ASC("\"), ASC("/"), ASC(":")
        LENGTH = PLACE
    END SELECT
  NEXT
  TEMPORARY = LEFT$(FILE_NAME, LENGTH) + "EDIT.$$$"
  CR_LF(0) = KEYS.ENTER
  CR_LF(1) = LF
  EDITED_FILE = DOS.CREATE_FILE(TEMPORARY, 0)
  CODE = DOS.ERROR
  IF CODE = 0 THEN
    CODE = WRITE_PART(0, GAP_POSITION)
    IF CODE = 0 THEN
      CODE = WRITE_PART(GAP_POSITION + GAP_SIZE, TEXT_LENGTH - GAP_POSITION)
    END IF
    DOS.CLOSE_FILE(EDITED_FILE)
    IF CODE = 0 THEN CODE = DOS.ERROR
    IF CODE = 0 THEN CODE = CLEAR_OLD()
    IF CODE = 0 THEN
      ' The file is gone, so a failed rename keeps EDIT.$$$.
      DOS.RENAME(TEMPORARY, FILE_NAME)
      CODE = DOS.ERROR
    ELSE
      DOS.DELETE(TEMPORARY)
    END IF
  END IF
  IF CODE = 0 THEN
    MODIFIED = 0
    MESSAGE = "Saved"
    ADD_RECENT()
  ELSEIF CODE = DOS.DISK_FULL THEN
    MESSAGE = "Insufficient disk space"
  ELSE
    MESSAGE = DOS.ERRMSG(CODE)
  END IF
  RETURN CODE
END FUNCT



' The dialogs and the menus run from GUI.UXI's region 2, beside the GUI's own, so their
' strings take no low RAM.
#REGION_SLOT 2
' Shows the Find dialog, or with CHANGING = 1 the Change dialog, with FIND_TEXT, CHANGE_TEXT
' for Change, and the check boxes of MATCH_CASE and WHOLE_WORD. Returns 1 for OK or Change
' All, and for Enter in the last field; else Cancel or Esc.
FUNCT ASK_FIND(CHANGING AS UBYTE) AS UBYTE
  DIM ROW AS UBYTE, FIRST AS UBYTE
  GUI.DIALOG_WIDTH = FIND_CAPTION + 1 + FIND_WIDTH
  ROW = 4
  IF CHANGING = 1 THEN
    GUI.OPEN_DIALOG("Change", 5, "Change &All", "&Cancel")
    ROW = 5
  ELSE
    GUI.OPEN_DIALOG("Find", 4, "&OK", "&Cancel")
  END IF
  ' The fields come last, so Enter in the last field returns EV_DONE.
  GUI.CHECK(ROW, 3, "Match Upper/Lowercase", @MATCH_CASE)
  GUI.CHECK(ROW + 1, 3, "Whole Word", @WHOLE_WORD)
  FIRST = GUI.SAYGET(2, 3, "Find What:", FIND_TEXT, FIND_WIDTH)
  IF CHANGING = 1 THEN GUI.SAYGET(3, 3, "Change To:", CHANGE_TEXT, FIND_WIDTH)
  RETURN GUI.RUN_DIALOG(FIRST)
END FUNCT



' Shows the Display dialog, with the radio buttons of THEME_CHOICE and TAB_CHOICE. OK uses
' them, writes them to C:\6502DOS.INI and asks for the screen; Cancel and Esc put them back.
SUB ASK_DISPLAY()
  DIM OLD_THEME AS UBYTE, OLD_TABS AS UBYTE, FIRST AS UBYTE
  OLD_THEME = THEME_CHOICE
  OLD_TABS = TAB_CHOICE
  ' A caption of 10 columns, a space, and the 27 columns of the colors.
  GUI.DIALOG_WIDTH = 38
  GUI.OPEN_DIALOG("Display", 2, "&OK", "&Cancel")
  FIRST = GUI.RADIO(2, 3, "Colors:   ", "Gray|Dark|Light", @THEME_CHOICE)
  GUI.RADIO(3, 3, "Tab Stops:", "8|4|3|2", @TAB_CHOICE)
  IF GUI.RUN_DIALOG(FIRST) = 1 THEN
    USE_DISPLAY()
    WRITE_DISPLAY()
    NEED_SCREEN = 1
  ELSE
    THEME_CHOICE = OLD_THEME
    TAB_CHOICE = OLD_TABS
  END IF
END SUB



' Puts the gap after the text, and the cursor and the page at its start, clears MODIFIED, and
' asks for the screen to be drawn again. For a text just loaded or emptied.
SUB START_TEXT()
  GAP_POSITION = TEXT_LENGTH
  GAP_SIZE = ROOM - TEXT_LENGTH
  CURSOR = 0
  CURSOR_LINE = 0
  LINE_BEGIN = 0
  TOP = 0
  TOP_LINE = 0
  LEFT_COLUMN = 0
  MODIFIED = 0
  NEED_SCREEN = 1
END SUB



' Makes the text an empty UNTITLED, with NEW_ENDS line ends. START_TEXT is still to be called.
SUB MAKE_UNTITLED()
  FILE_NAME = "UNTITLED"
  NAMED = 0
  TEXT_LENGTH = 0
  CR_ENDS = NEW_ENDS
END SUB



' Asks the file name in the file dialog, and saves the text under it. A file that exists is
' replaced only after Yes. Returns 0 when it saved; else FILE_NAME is kept, and MESSAGE holds
' the error of a save that failed.
FUNCT SAVE_AS() AS UBYTE
  DIM CODE AS UBYTE
  IF GUI.PICKFILE("Save As", "*.TXT", PICKED) = 0 THEN RETURN 1
  EDITED_FILE = DOS.OPEN_FILE(PICKED, DOS.ACCESS_READ)
  IF EDITED_FILE <> NOFILE THEN
    DOS.CLOSE_FILE(EDITED_FILE)
    IF GUI.YESNO("Save As", "The file already exists.", "Replace it?") = 0 THEN RETURN 1
  END IF
  KEPT = FILE_NAME
  FILE_NAME = PICKED
  CODE = SAVE()
  IF CODE = 0 THEN
    NAMED = 1
    NEED_SCREEN = 1
  ELSE
    FILE_NAME = KEPT
  END IF
  RETURN CODE
END FUNCT



' Saves the text under FILE_NAME, or by SAVE_AS when it is UNTITLED. Returns 0 when it saved.
FUNCT SAVE_FILE() AS UBYTE
  IF NAMED = 1 THEN RETURN SAVE()
  RETURN SAVE_AS()
END FUNCT



' Asks in a dialog whether to save the text when it has changed. Yes saves, No does not, and
' Esc goes back to the text. Returns 1 to go on: always for text with no changes, after No,
' or after Yes when the save worked.
FUNCT ASK_SAVE() AS UBYTE
  IF MODIFIED = 0 THEN RETURN 1
  SELECT CASE GUI.MSGBOX("EDIT", "The text has changed.", "Save it now?", "", "&Yes", "&No")
    CASE 1
      RETURN SAVE_FILE() = 0
    CASE 2
      RETURN 1
  END SELECT
  RETURN 0
END FUNCT



' Loads recent file RECENT, 1 to 4, or with RECENT 0 a file asked in the file dialog, in place
' of the text, after ASK_SAVE. A file that does not load shows its error in a dialog.
SUB OPEN_TEXT(RECENT AS UBYTE)
  DIM CHOSEN AS STRING * 80, CODE AS UBYTE
  ' The recent file is named before ASK_SAVE, whose save may change the recent files.
  IF RECENT <> 0 THEN RECENT_NAME(RECENT, CHOSEN)
  IF ASK_SAVE() = 0 THEN RETURN
  IF RECENT = 0 THEN
    IF GUI.PICKFILE("Open", "*.TXT", CHOSEN) = 0 THEN RETURN
  END IF
  KEPT = FILE_NAME
  FILE_NAME = CHOSEN
  CODE = LOAD()
  IF CODE = TOO_LARGE THEN
    GUI.MSGBOX("Open", "File too large")
  ELSEIF CODE <> 0 THEN
    GUI.MSGBOX("Open", DOS.ERRMSG(CODE))
  END IF
  IF CODE <> 0 THEN
    IF EDITED_FILE = NOFILE THEN
      FILE_NAME = KEPT
      RETURN
    END IF
    MAKE_UNTITLED()
  ELSE
    NAMED = 1
    ADD_RECENT()
  END IF
  START_TEXT()
END SUB



' The key that does the menu item ID: the id itself for an item a control key does. New, Open,
' Save As, Display and About, which no key does, are done here and give 0, no key.
FUNCT MENU_KEY(ID AS UBYTE) AS UWORD
  SELECT CASE ID
    CASE ID_CLEAR
      RETURN KEYS.KEY_DELETE
    CASE ID_DOS_HELP
      RETURN KEYS.KEY_SHIFT_F1
    CASE ID_FIND_AGAIN
      RETURN KEY_F3
    CASE ID_NEW
      IF ASK_SAVE() = 1 THEN
        MAKE_UNTITLED()
        START_TEXT()
      END IF
    CASE ID_OPEN
      OPEN_TEXT(0)
    CASE ID_RECENT TO ID_RECENT + 3
      OPEN_TEXT(ID - ID_RECENT + 1)
    CASE ID_SAVE_AS
      SAVE_AS()
    CASE ID_DISPLAY
      ASK_DISPLAY()
    CASE ID_ABOUT
      GUI.MSGBOX("About", "EDIT, the 6502DOS Editor", "F10 or Alt+letter opens a menu.")
    CASE ELSE
      RETURN ID
  END SELECT
  RETURN 0
END FUNCT




' Makes EDIT_FORM, the form that fills the screen between the menu bar and the status row,
' titled FILE_NAME, and its menus.
SUB MAKE_MENUS()
  EDIT_FORM = GUI.CREATEFORM(FILE_NAME, 1, 0, 80, 28, GUI.FRAMED OR GUI.NO_SHADOW)
  MAKE_BAR()
END SUB



' Makes EDIT_FORM's menu bar and its menus. The File menu holds the recent files that are not
' "", between separators.
SUB MAKE_BAR()
  GUI.MENUBAR(EDIT_FORM)
  GUI.BEGINMENU("&File")
  GUI.MENUITEM("&New", ID_NEW)
  GUI.MENUITEM("&Open...", ID_OPEN)
  GUI.MENUITEM("&Save      Ctrl+S", CTRL_S)
  GUI.MENUITEM("Save &As...", ID_SAVE_AS)
  IF LEN(RECENT_1) <> 0 THEN
    GUI.MENUITEM("-", 0)
    GUI.MENUITEM(RECENT_1, ID_RECENT)
    IF LEN(RECENT_2) <> 0 THEN GUI.MENUITEM(RECENT_2, ID_RECENT + 1)
    IF LEN(RECENT_3) <> 0 THEN GUI.MENUITEM(RECENT_3, ID_RECENT + 2)
    IF LEN(RECENT_4) <> 0 THEN GUI.MENUITEM(RECENT_4, ID_RECENT + 3)
  END IF
  GUI.MENUITEM("-", 0)
  GUI.MENUITEM("E&xit      Ctrl+Q", CTRL_Q)
  GUI.ENDMENU()
  GUI.BEGINMENU("&Edit")
  GUI.MENUITEM("Cu&t       Ctrl+X", CTRL_X)
  GUI.MENUITEM("&Copy      Ctrl+C", CTRL_C)
  GUI.MENUITEM("&Paste     Ctrl+V", CTRL_V)
  GUI.MENUITEM("Cl&ear     Del", ID_CLEAR)
  GUI.ENDMENU()
  GUI.BEGINMENU("&Search")
  GUI.MENUITEM("&Find...            Ctrl+F", CTRL_F)
  GUI.MENUITEM("&Repeat Last Find       F3", ID_FIND_AGAIN)
  GUI.MENUITEM("&Change...          Ctrl+R", CTRL_R)
  GUI.ENDMENU()
  GUI.BEGINMENU("&Options")
  GUI.MENUITEM("&Display...", ID_DISPLAY)
  GUI.ENDMENU()
  GUI.BEGINMENU("&Help")
  GUI.MENUITEM("&DOS Help  Shift+F1", ID_DOS_HELP)
  GUI.MENUITEM("&About", ID_ABOUT)
  GUI.ENDMENU()
END SUB



' The settings run from region 5.
#REGION_SLOT 5
#INCLUDE "INI.UXI"
' Sets EDIT's options from the section [EDIT] of C:\6502DOS.INI. A key that is missing, or has
' another value, takes the default in brackets. THEME is DARK, LIGHT or [GRAY]. TABS is 2, 3, 4
' or [8]. MATCHCASE and WHOLEWORD are 1 or [0]. FIND is the text to find, [none]. LINEENDS is a new
' file's line ends, [CRLF] or LF. BAK is 1 to keep the old file as a .BAK on a save, or [0].
' RECENT is the recent files, separated by |, [none].
SUB READ_SETTINGS()
  DIM VALUE AS STRING * 8, LIST AS STRING * 255
  VALUE = UCASE$(INI.READ_KEY$("EDIT", "THEME", ""))
  THEME_CHOICE = 0
  IF VALUE = "DARK" THEN THEME_CHOICE = 1
  IF VALUE = "LIGHT" THEN THEME_CHOICE = 2
  VALUE = INI.READ_KEY$("EDIT", "TABS", "")
  TAB_CHOICE = 0
  IF VALUE = "4" THEN TAB_CHOICE = 1
  IF VALUE = "3" THEN TAB_CHOICE = 2
  IF VALUE = "2" THEN TAB_CHOICE = 3
  USE_DISPLAY()
  MATCH_CASE = 0
  IF INI.READ_KEY$("EDIT", "MATCHCASE", "") = "1" THEN MATCH_CASE = 1
  WHOLE_WORD = 0
  IF INI.READ_KEY$("EDIT", "WHOLEWORD", "") = "1" THEN WHOLE_WORD = 1
  FIND_TEXT = INI.READ_KEY$("EDIT", "FIND", "")
  NEW_ENDS = 1
  IF UCASE$(INI.READ_KEY$("EDIT", "LINEENDS", "")) = "LF" THEN NEW_ENDS = 0
  BACKUP = 0
  IF INI.READ_KEY$("EDIT", "BAK", "") = "1" THEN BACKUP = 1
  LIST = INI.READ_KEY$("EDIT", "RECENT", "")
  NEXT_RECENT(LIST, RECENT_1, ASC("1"))
  NEXT_RECENT(LIST, RECENT_2, ASC("2"))
  NEXT_RECENT(LIST, RECENT_3, ASC("3"))
  NEXT_RECENT(LIST, RECENT_4, ASC("4"))
END SUB



' Takes the first name off LIST, up to its | or its end, and sets CAPTION to the caption of
' recent file DIGIT with that name, or to "" for an empty name.
SUB NEXT_RECENT(LIST AS STRING, CAPTION AS STRING, DIGIT AS UBYTE)
  DIM BAR AS UBYTE
  BAR = INSTR(LIST, "|")
  IF BAR = 0 THEN BAR = LEN(LIST) + 1
  CAPTION = ""
  IF BAR > 1 THEN CAPTION = "&" + CHR$(DIGIT) + " " + LEFT$(LIST, BAR - 1)
  LIST = MID$(LIST, BAR + 1)
END SUB



' Sets NAME to the path of recent file NUMBER, 1 to 4.
SUB RECENT_NAME(NUMBER AS UBYTE, NAME AS STRING)
  IF NUMBER = 1 THEN NAME = MID$(RECENT_1, 4)
  IF NUMBER = 2 THEN NAME = MID$(RECENT_2, 4)
  IF NUMBER = 3 THEN NAME = MID$(RECENT_3, 4)
  IF NUMBER = 4 THEN NAME = MID$(RECENT_4, 4)
END SUB



' Puts FILE_NAME first in the recent files, as a full path in capitals, and writes them to
' RECENT in [EDIT]. The same name further down, or else the fourth, leaves the list. A name
' already first, or longer than 60 characters, changes nothing. The menu bar is made again
' once EDIT_FORM is not 0.
SUB ADD_RECENT()
  DIM TEXT AS STRING * 250, DROP AS UBYTE
  ' A name with no drive takes the current drive, and one that does not start with \ or / that
  ' drive's current folder too. SET_PATH gives them from the drive letter to a closing \.
  TEXT = FILE_NAME
  IF MID$(TEXT, 2, 1) <> ":" THEN
    GUI.SET_PATH(DOS.GETDRIVE() + 1)
    IF ASC(TEXT) = ASC("\") OR ASC(TEXT) = ASC("/") THEN
      TEXT = LEFT$(DOS.CALL_TEXT, 2) + TEXT
    ELSE
      TEXT = DOS.CALL_TEXT + TEXT
    END IF
  END IF
  TEXT = UCASE$(TEXT)
  IF LEN(TEXT) > 60 OR TEXT = MID$(RECENT_1, 4) THEN RETURN
  DROP = 4
  IF TEXT = MID$(RECENT_2, 4) THEN DROP = 2
  IF TEXT = MID$(RECENT_3, 4) THEN DROP = 3
  IF DROP = 4 THEN RECENT_4 = RECENT_3
  IF DROP >= 3 THEN RECENT_3 = RECENT_2
  RECENT_2 = RECENT_1
  RECENT_1 = "&1 " + TEXT
  ' A caption's digit is its second character.
  IF LEN(RECENT_2) <> 0 THEN ContentsAt(@RECENT_2 + 3) = ASC("2")
  IF LEN(RECENT_3) <> 0 THEN ContentsAt(@RECENT_3 + 3) = ASC("3")
  IF LEN(RECENT_4) <> 0 THEN ContentsAt(@RECENT_4 + 3) = ASC("4")
  TEXT = MID$(RECENT_1, 4) + "|" + MID$(RECENT_2, 4) + "|" + MID$(RECENT_3, 4) + "|" + MID$(RECENT_4, 4)
  INI.WRITE_KEY("EDIT", "RECENT", TEXT)
  IF EDIT_FORM <> 0 THEN MAKE_BAR()
END SUB



' Sets the theme from THEME_CHOICE, and TAB_SIZE from TAB_CHOICE.
SUB USE_DISPLAY()
  IF THEME_CHOICE = 1 THEN
    GUI.THEME(DARK)
  ELSEIF THEME_CHOICE = 2 THEN
    GUI.THEME(LIGHT)
  ELSE
    GUI.THEME(GRAY)
  END IF
  TAB_SIZE = 8 >> TAB_CHOICE
  IF TAB_CHOICE >= 2 THEN TAB_SIZE = 5 - TAB_CHOICE
END SUB



' Writes THEME and TABS to [EDIT] from THEME_CHOICE and TAB_CHOICE.
SUB WRITE_DISPLAY()
  DIM VALUE AS STRING * 8
  VALUE = "GRAY"
  IF THEME_CHOICE = 1 THEN VALUE = "DARK"
  IF THEME_CHOICE = 2 THEN VALUE = "LIGHT"
  INI.WRITE_KEY("EDIT", "THEME", VALUE)
  INI.WRITE_KEY("EDIT", "TABS", CHR$(48 + TAB_SIZE))
END SUB



' Moves FILE_NAME out of the way of a save. With BACKUP = 1 it is renamed to its name with the
' extension .BAK, after the old .BAK is deleted; else, or when the file is a .BAK, it is
' deleted. A file that does not exist is no error. Returns 0 or the error number.
FUNCT CLEAR_OLD() AS UBYTE
  DIM BACKUP_NAME AS STRING * 84, DOT AS UBYTE, PLACE AS UBYTE, CODE AS UBYTE
  IF BACKUP = 1 THEN
    ' DOT ends as the place of the last . after the last \, / or :, or 0.
    DOT = 0
    FOR PLACE = 1 TO LEN(FILE_NAME)
      SELECT CASE ContentsAt(@FILE_NAME + 1 + PLACE)
        CASE ASC(".")
          DOT = PLACE
        CASE ASC("\"), ASC("/"), ASC(":")
          DOT = 0
      END SELECT
    NEXT
    IF DOT = 0 THEN DOT = LEN(FILE_NAME) + 1
    BACKUP_NAME = LEFT$(FILE_NAME, DOT - 1) + ".BAK"
    IF UCASE$(BACKUP_NAME) <> UCASE$(FILE_NAME) THEN
      DOS.DELETE(BACKUP_NAME)
      DOS.RENAME(FILE_NAME, BACKUP_NAME)
      CODE = DOS.ERROR
      IF CODE = DOS.ERR_NOT_FOUND THEN CODE = 0
      RETURN CODE
    END IF
  END IF
  DOS.DELETE(FILE_NAME)
  CODE = DOS.ERROR
  IF CODE = DOS.ERR_NOT_FOUND THEN CODE = 0
  RETURN CODE
END FUNCT
#REGION_SLOT 0




'--- program starts here -------------------------------------------
FILE_NAME = HEAP.SYS_STRINGS_GET(SLOT_P1)
IF HEAP.SYS_STRINGS_GET(SLOT_P2) <> "" THEN
  PRINT "Too many parameters"
  END 1
END IF
EDIT_FORM = 0
BANK_COUNT = 0
ROOM = 0
READ_SETTINGS()
IF FILE_NAME = "" THEN
  MAKE_UNTITLED()
ELSE
  NAMED = 1
  CR_ENDS = NEW_ENDS
  QUIT = LOAD()
  IF QUIT = 0 THEN ADD_RECENT()
  IF QUIT = DOS.ERR_NOT_FOUND THEN
    MESSAGE = "New file"
    QUIT = 0
  ELSEIF QUIT = TOO_LARGE THEN
    PRINT "File too large"
  ELSEIF QUIT <> 0 THEN
    PRINT DOS.ERRMSG(QUIT)
  END IF
  IF QUIT <> 0 THEN END 2
END IF
START_TEXT()
DOS.STOP_KEY(DOS.STOP.OFF)
START_COLOR = DOS.GET_COLOR()
MAKE_MENUS()
FOLLOW_CURSOR()
DRAW()
PENDING = 0
DO
  IF PENDING <> 0 THEN
    KEY = PENDING
    PENDING = 0
  ELSE
    KEY = WAITKEY()
  END IF
  MODIFIERS = KEYMODS()
  MESSAGE = ""
  ' F10 and Alt with a letter open a menu; the item chosen gives its key, and Esc no key.
  IF KEY = KEYS.KEY_F10 OR GUI.ALT_LETTER(KEY) <> 0 THEN
    KEY = MENU_KEY(GUI.PULL_MENU(EDIT_FORM, KEY))
  END IF
  VERTICAL = 0
  NAVIGATING = 0
  OLD_LINE = CURSOR_LINE
  ' SELECTION_BEGIN and SELECTION_END keep an ended selection for Ctrl+X.
  SELECT CASE KEY
    CASE KEYS.KEY_HOME, KEYS.KEY_UP, KEYS.KEY_PGUP, KEYS.KEY_LEFT, KEYS.KEY_RIGHT, _
         KEYS.KEY_END, KEYS.KEY_DOWN, KEYS.KEY_PGDN
      NAVIGATING = 1
      IF MODIFIERS AND KEYS.MOD_SHIFT THEN
        IF SELECTING = 0 THEN ANCHOR = CURSOR
        SELECTING = 1
      ELSE
        SELECTING = 0
      END IF
    CASE ELSE
      IF KEY <> CTRL_C THEN SELECTING = 0
  END SELECT
  SELECT CASE KEY
    CASE KEYS.KEY_LEFT
      IF CURSOR > 0 THEN
        CURSOR = CURSOR - 1
        IF CURSOR < LINE_BEGIN THEN LINE_UP()
      END IF
    CASE KEYS.KEY_RIGHT
      IF CURSOR < TEXT_LENGTH THEN
        IF BYTE_AT(CURSOR) = LF THEN LINE_DOWN()
        CURSOR = CURSOR + 1
      END IF
    CASE KEYS.KEY_HOME
      CURSOR = LINE_BEGIN
    CASE KEYS.KEY_END
      CURSOR = LINE_END(CURSOR)
    CASE KEYS.KEY_UP
      VERTICAL = 1
      IF LINE_UP() = 1 THEN CURSOR = POSITION_AT(LINE_BEGIN, GOAL)
    CASE KEYS.KEY_DOWN
      VERTICAL = 1
      IF LINE_DOWN() = 1 THEN CURSOR = POSITION_AT(LINE_BEGIN, GOAL)
    CASE KEYS.KEY_PGUP
      ' The page moves as far as the cursor, and no further than the first line.
      VERTICAL = 1
      FOR STEPS = 1 TO TEXT_ROWS
        IF LINE_UP() = 0 THEN EXIT FOR
        IF TOP_LINE > 0 THEN
          TOP = LINE_START(TOP - 1)
          TOP_LINE = TOP_LINE - 1
          NEED_PAGE = 1
        END IF
      NEXT
      CURSOR = POSITION_AT(LINE_BEGIN, GOAL)
    CASE KEYS.KEY_PGDN
      VERTICAL = 1
      FOR STEPS = 1 TO TEXT_ROWS
        IF LINE_DOWN() = 0 THEN EXIT FOR
        TOP = LINE_END(TOP) + 1
        TOP_LINE = TOP_LINE + 1
        NEED_PAGE = 1
      NEXT
      CURSOR = POSITION_AT(LINE_BEGIN, GOAL)
    CASE KEYS.KEY_SHIFT_F1
      SHOW_DOS_HELP()
    CASE KEYS.KEY_DELETE
      IF SELECTION_END > SELECTION_BEGIN THEN
        REMOVE_PART(SELECTION_BEGIN, SELECTION_END)
      ELSEIF CURSOR < TEXT_LENGTH THEN
        IF BYTE_AT(CURSOR) = LF THEN
          NEED_PAGE = 1
        ELSE
          CHANGED_ROW()
        END IF
        REMOVE(CURSOR)
      END IF
    CASE KEYS.ENTER
      INSERT(LF)
    CASE KEYS.TAB
      INSERT(KEYS.TAB)
    CASE CTRL_Q
      QUIT = ASK_SAVE()
    CASE CTRL_S
      SAVE_FILE()
    CASE CTRL_C
      TAKE(0)
    CASE CTRL_X
      TAKE(1)
    CASE CTRL_V
      PASTE()
    CASE CTRL_F
      IF ASK_FIND(0) = 1 THEN FIND_AGAIN()
    CASE KEY_F3
      FIND_AGAIN()
    CASE CTRL_R
      IF ASK_FIND(1) = 1 THEN CHANGE_ALL()
    CASE KEYS.BACKSPACE
      IF SELECTION_END > SELECTION_BEGIN THEN
        REMOVE_PART(SELECTION_BEGIN, SELECTION_END)
      ELSEIF CURSOR > 0 THEN
        CURSOR = CURSOR - 1
        IF CURSOR < LINE_BEGIN THEN
          LINE_UP()
          NEED_PAGE = 1
        ELSE
          CHANGED_ROW()
        END IF
        REMOVE(CURSOR)
      END IF
    CASE KEYS.SPACE TO 255
      INSERT(KEY)
  END SELECT
  ' A changed selection draws the cursor's row again when the cursor stayed on its line, else
  ' the page.
  NEW_BEGIN = 0
  NEW_END = 0
  IF SELECTING = 1 THEN
    IF ANCHOR < CURSOR THEN
      NEW_BEGIN = ANCHOR
      NEW_END = CURSOR
    ELSE
      NEW_BEGIN = CURSOR
      NEW_END = ANCHOR
    END IF
  END IF
  IF NEW_BEGIN <> SELECTION_BEGIN OR NEW_END <> SELECTION_END THEN
    IF SELECTING = 1 AND CURSOR_LINE = OLD_LINE THEN
      CHANGED_ROW()
    ELSE
      NEED_PAGE = 1
    END IF
    SELECTION_BEGIN = NEW_BEGIN
    SELECTION_END = NEW_END
  END IF
  FOLLOW_CURSOR()
  ' After an arrow or page key, the repeats of that key that wait are dropped, so a held key
  ' stops where it is let go. The first other key waits in PENDING. The page is drawn only when
  ' no key waits, so typing does not outrun it.
  IF NAVIGATING = 1 THEN
    DO
      PENDING = GETEXTKEY()
    LOOP WHILE PENDING = KEY
  END IF
  SYS DOS.API_CON_STATUS
  IF DOS.REG_A = 0 AND PENDING = 0 AND QUIT = 0 THEN DRAW()
LOOP UNTIL QUIT = 1
DOS.SET_COLOR(START_COLOR)
PRINT CONS.CLEAR_SCREEN$; "EDIT - The 6502DOS Editor... Bye!"
END 0
